      "source": [
        {
          "question": "e-5966",
          "field": null,
          "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
          "value": "First, we find the value of the function at $P\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n  f\\left(\\pi,1,\\dfrac{1}{2}\\right)&= \\sin \\left(\\pi\\cdot 1 \\cdot \\dfrac{1}{2} \\right) = \\sin{\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{2}\\right)} = 1}\n$$\n\nRecall that the level surfaces for the function $f(x,y,z)$ are given by the equation\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z) = c.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we're interested in $c = 1.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y,z) & =c \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}\u2061xyz & =1 \\\\ xyz & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}+2\\pi k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $k$ is any integer.\n\nTherefore, the level surface that passes through the point $P\\left(\\pi,1,\\dfrac{1}{2}\\right)$ is the surface $xyz= \\dfrac{\\pi}{2} + 2\\pi k,$ where $k$ is any integer.",
          "category": "ma_capture",
